# RFC-LOC-1 PR4: `npm run sample:v2` regenerates the V2 public sample byte for byte, with LF line endings.
# Keep LF in every checkout so the committed files and the generator output stay identical on Windows clones with
# core.autocrlf=true. The two legacy samples are the generator's input: the fixed identity manifest records the
# sha256 of their raw bytes, so their line endings must not depend on the checkout either.
01_Web/src/data/v2-sample/*.json text eol=lf
01_Web/src/data/travel-map.sample.json text eol=lf
01_Web/src/data/want-to-go.sample.json text eol=lf
